---

<section id="lifecycle" class="section band">
  <div class="wrap lifecycle">
    <h2 class="h2" data-reveal>Nothing to clean up.</h2>
    <p class="body" data-reveal style="--rd: 0.06s">
      Sensus runs as a child of your shell, never <code>exec</code>'d. Exit (or detach with
      <code>Ctrl+A d</code>) and you are back at a plain prompt: the shells and the agent's work
      keep running in the local daemon, re-attachable on the next boot. Closing a tab never kills
      its shell; type <code>exit</code> in the pane to end one. When you want a clean slate,
      <code>sensus kill</code> is the kill switch: one command stops every local daemon and the
      shells they own.
    </p>
    <div
      class="transcript mono"
      aria-label="Detaching and reattaching leaves everything running"
      data-reveal-print
    >
      <div class="line">
        <span class="prompt">❯</span> sensus
        <span class="comment"># the TUI opens; shells run in the local daemon</span>
      </div>
      <div class="line ellipsis">…</div>
      <div class="line">
        <span class="prompt">❯</span> Ctrl+A d
        <span class="comment"># detach: back to this prompt, nothing killed</span>
      </div>
      <div class="line">
        <span class="prompt">❯</span> sensus
        <span class="comment"># reattach: tabs, shells, and sessions are still there</span>
      </div>
      <div class="line">
        <span class="prompt">❯</span> sensus kill
        <span class="comment"># kill switch: stop every local daemon and its shells</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .lifecycle {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    justify-items: center;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .lifecycle .body {
    max-width: 70ch;
  }

  .transcript {
    width: min(100%, 780px);
    margin-top: 1rem;
    padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background: var(--bg);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    text-align: left;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 2;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .line {
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .prompt {
    color: var(--success);
    margin-right: 0.5rem;
  }

  .comment {
    margin-left: 0.6rem;
    color: var(--fg-faint);
  }

  .ellipsis {
    color: var(--fg-faint);
    user-select: none;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .transcript {
      font-size: 0.75rem;
    }

    .line {
      white-space: normal;
      text-wrap: pretty;
    }
  }
</style>
